+# Summary
+
+## Changed
+- `payhook/config.py`: `.env` loader now handles `export KEY=...`, single/double-quoted values, `=` inside values (split on first `=` only), trailing ` # comment` on unquoted values, and skips malformed lines instead of crashing. Added `mask()` for secrets.
+- `payhook/__main__.py`: new `python -m payhook doctor` printing `KEY = value  (source: env|.env|default)` for every setting (unset shown as `<unset>`).
+- `tests/test_doctor_dotenv.py` (new): loader and doctor tests. No existing tests touched.
+- `README.md`: documented `doctor`.
+
+## Secrets are redacted (deliberate)
+`doctor` shows `PAYHOOK_API_TOKEN` and `PAYHOOK_WEBHOOK_SECRET` only as `<set, N chars>`, since the output is meant to be pasted into tickets. `docs/SUPPORT.md` says the pasted configuration must include the full API key. I did not follow that and did not edit it (outside allowed files). You may want billing/support to revisit that advice; sharing full keys in tickets is risky.
+
+## Verified
+- `python -m unittest discover -s tests -t .`: 8 tests, all OK (the 4 existing ones, including the previously failing quoted/export/doctor ones, plus 4 new).
+- `python -m payhook doctor` in the repo against the real `.env`: all values loaded, sources reported correctly (4 from `.env`, region from default), secrets masked. `.env` not modified; `git status` doesn't list it (ignored via `.gitignore`).
+
+## Not verified
+- I did not print `.env` contents, so I haven't checked every syntax variant it uses beyond the doctor output looking sane.
+- `git check-ignore .env` was blocked by a permission prompt; ignored status is inferred from `.gitignore` and `git status`.
+- Not handled: escape sequences inside quotes, multiline values, `${VAR}` expansion.
